  "landfallEstimate": "Tracking over Bay of Bengal; Doppler radars monitoring",
  "rawBulletin": "REGIONAL SPECIALISED METEOROLOGICAL CENTRE -TROPICAL CYCLONES,\nNEW DELHI TROPICAL CYCLONE ADVISORY NO 32\nDEMS-RSMC TROPICAL CYCLONES NEW DELHI DATED 20.11.2026\nFROM: RSMC \u2013TROPICAL CYCLONES, NEW DELHI\nTO: STORM WARNING CENTRE, NAYPYITAW (MYANMAR)\nSTORM WARNING CENTRE, BANGKOK (THAILAND)\nSTORM WARNING CENTRE, COLOMBO (SRILANKA)\nSTORM WARNING CENTRE, DHAKA (BANGLADESH)\nSTORM WARNING CENTRE, KARACHI (PAKISTAN)\nMETEOROLOGICAL OFFICE, MALE (MALDIVES)\nOMAN METEOROLOGICAL DEPARTMENT,\nMUSCAT (THROUGH RTH JEDDAH)\nYEMEN METEOROLOGICAL SERVICES,\nREPUBLIC OF YEMEN (THROUGH RTH JEDDAH)\nNATIONAL CENTRE FOR METEOROLOGY, UAE (THROUGH RTH JEDDAH)\nPRESIDENCY OF METEOROLOGY AND ENVIRONMENT,\nSAUDI ARABIA (THROUGH RTH JEDDAH)\nIRAN METEOROLOGICAL ORGANISATION, (THROUGH RTH JEDDAH)\nQATAR METEOROLOGICAL DEPARTMENT (THROUGH RTH JEDDAH)\nTROPICAL CYCLONE ADVISORY NO. 32 FOR THE NORTH INDIAN OCEAN\n(THE BAY OF BENGAL AND THE ARABIAN SEA) VALID FOR THE NEXT 168\nHOURS ISSUED AT 1500 UTC OF 20.11.2026 BASED ON 1200 UTC OF\n20.11.2026.\nSub: Deep Depression (Remnant of Severe Cyclonic Storm \u201cAkvan\u201d) weakened into a\nDepression over south Odisha.\nThe Deep Depression (Remnant of Severe Cyclonic Storm \u201cAkvan\u201d) over south coastal\nOdisha moved northwards with a speed of 12 kmph during past 06 hours, weakened into a\nDepression and lay centered at 1200 UTC of today, the 20th November, 2026, over south\nOdisha near latitude 20.2\u00b0N and longitude 84.9\u00b0E, about 70 km south-southwest of Angul\n(42969, Odisha), 100 km north of Gopalpur (43049,Odisha) and 110 km west-northwest of\nPuri (43053,Odisha).\nIt is likely to move nearly northwards over Odisha and weaken into a Well Marked Low\nPressure Area during next 06 hours.\nThe forecast location and intensity of the system is given below:\nDate/Time Position Maximum sustained Category of cyclonic\n(UTC) (Lat. 0N/ long. 0E) surface disturbance\nwind speed (Kmph)\n20.11.26/1200 20.2/84.9 40-50 gusting to 60 Depression\n20.11.26/1800 20.8/85.0 20-30 gusting to 40 Well Marked Low Pressure Area\nCloud distribution: (a) Isolated: <25%, Scattered:25-50%, Broken: 51-75%, Solid:>75%, Convection Intensity: (a) Weak:\nCloud Top Temperature(CTT)>-25\u00b0C, (b) Moderate: CTT:-25\u00b0Cto-40\u00b0C, (c) Intense: CTT: -41\u00b0Cto -70\u00b0C and (d) Very\nIntense::Less than -70\u00b0C Probability of cyclogenesis (formation of depression) :NIL:0%, LOW:1-33%, MODERATE:34-\n66% and HIGH:67-100%\nAs per INSAT 3DS, remnant of AKVAN vortex lay over the North Odisha & neighbourhood\nand the centre is not defined in satellite imagery. Associated scattered to broken low and\nmedium-level clouds, with embedded intense to very intense convection lay over North Bay\nof Bengal,Odisha, Gangetic West Bengal, north Chhattisgarh, northeast states and\nBangladesh (minimum Cloud-Top Temperature (CTT) ranges from -70\u00b0C to -90\u00b0C) and\nmoderate to intense convection over Central Bay of Bengal, North Costal Andhra Pradesh,\nChhattisgarh, Jharkhand, Bihar and Sub-Himalayan West Bengal (minimum CTT) ranges\nfrom -40\u00b0C to -70\u00b0C).\nThe estimated central pressure is 1006 hPa and maximum sustained wind speed is 25 kt\ngusting to 35 kt. Rough Sea condition is prevailing over Bay of Bengal.\nRemarks:\nMadden Julian Oscillation (MJO) is in phase 4 with amplitude more than 1. It is likely to\nphase 4 till 21st November. Thus, MJO is favorable for enhancement of convective activity\nover Bay of Bengal till 21st November. However, the decreasing amplitude of the MJO would\nbe reducing the support. Guidance from NCICS model indicates Easterly wind anomaly over\nBay of Bengal with presence of MJO over Bay of Bengal till 23rd November.\nThe upper level divergence has reduced and is around 20X10-5 Sec-1 and is oriented to the\nnortheast of the system centre and Low level convergence is around 20X10-5 Sec-1 and is\noriented to northwest of the system centre. The vertical wind shear is about 25-30 knots\naround the system area, which is not supporting maintenance of the system. The Low level\npositive vorticity is 50 X 10-5 Sec-1 at system centr",
